{
    "53261": {
        "order_id": 1,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "quadratic-equations",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) If p varies directly as \\(r^{2}\\) and p = 3.2 when&nbsp;r = 4, find the value of p when r = 6.5.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Solve the simultaneous equations :</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{y}{4} = 1 ; \\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{y}{4} = \\frac{-1}{6}\\)</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) \\(p \\propto r^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\implies p = kr^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(3.2 = k(4^{2}) \\implies 3.2 = 16k\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(k = \\frac{3.2}{16} = 0.2\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore p = 0.2r^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>When r = 6.5,</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(p = 0.2 (6.5^{2}) \\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(0.2(42.25)\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(p = 8.45\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) \\(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{y}{4} = 1 ... (1)\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{x}{3} - \\frac{y}{4} = -\\frac{1}{6}&nbsp; &nbsp;.... (2)\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Adding equation (1) and (2), we have</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{x}{2} + \\frac{x}{3} = 1 - \\frac{1}{6}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{5x}{6} = \\frac{5}{6} \\implies x = 1\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Put x = 1 in (1),</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{y}{4} = 1 \\implies \\frac{y}{4} = 1 - \\frac{1}{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{y}{4} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies y = 2\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\((x, y) = (1, 2)\\).</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "53263": {
        "order_id": 2,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "logarithms",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>Without using Mathematical tables or a calculator, simplify :</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) \\(\\sqrt{50} - 3\\sqrt{2}(2\\sqrt{2} - 5) - 5\\sqrt{32}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\log_{10} \\frac{25}{4} - 2 \\log_{10} \\frac{4}{5} + \\log_{10} \\frac{320}{125}\\).</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) \\(\\sqrt{50} - 3\\sqrt{2}(2\\sqrt{2} - 5) - 5\\sqrt{32}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\sqrt{25 \\times 2} - (3 \\times 2)\\sqrt{2 \\times 2} +&nbsp;(3 \\times 5)\\sqrt{2} - 5\\sqrt{16 \\times 2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(5\\sqrt{2} - 6(2) +&nbsp;15\\sqrt{2} - 5(4\\sqrt{2})\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(5\\sqrt{2} - 12 +&nbsp;15\\sqrt{2} - 20\\sqrt{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\((5 + 15 - 20)\\sqrt{2} - 12\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= -12.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\log_{10} (\\frac{25}{4}) - 2 \\log_{10} (\\frac{4}{5}) + \\log_{10} (\\frac{320}{125})\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\log_{10} (\\frac{25}{4})^{\\frac{1}{2}} - \\log_{10} (\\frac{4}{5})^{2} + \\log_{10} (\\frac{320}{125})\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\log_{10} (\\frac{5}{2}) - \\log_{10} (\\frac{16}{25}) + \\log_{10} (\\frac{320}{125})\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\log_{10} (\\frac{\\frac{5}{2} \\times \\frac{320}{125}}{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\log_{10} (\\frac{\\frac{160}{25}}{\\frac{16}{25}}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\log_{10} 10&nbsp;= 1\\)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 1,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "53265": {
        "order_id": 3,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "trigonometric-ratios",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>(a) Simplify : \\(625^{\\frac{3}{8}} \\times 5^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\div 25\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Solve the following equations correct to one decimal place.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(i) \\(\\tan (\\theta + 25)&deg; = 5.145\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) \\(5\\cos \\theta - 1 = 0\\), where \\(0&deg; \\leq \\theta \\leq 90&deg;\\).</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) \\(625^{\\frac{3}{8}} \\times 5^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\div 25\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\((5^{4})^{\\frac{3}{8}} \\times 5^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\div 5^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(5^{\\frac{3}{2}} \\times 5^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\div 5^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(5^{\\frac{3}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} - 2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(5^{0} = 1\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b)(i) \\(\\tan (\\theta + 25)&deg; = 5.145\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta + 25&nbsp;= \\tan^{-1} (5.145)\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\implies \\theta + 25&nbsp;= 79&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta&nbsp; = 79&deg; - 25&deg; = 54&deg;\\)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) \\(5 \\cos \\theta - 1 = 0\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\implies 5 \\cos \\theta = 1\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\cos \\theta = \\frac{1}{5} = 0.2\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = \\cos^{-1} (0.2) = 78.463&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\approxeq 78.5&deg;\\) (to one d.p)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 2,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "53267": {
        "order_id": 4,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "geometry-and-trigonometry",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan (2)(7).jpg\" style=\"height:258px; width:250px\" />&nbsp; In the diagram, PQRS is a circle with centre O and radius 7cm. SQ and PR intersect at K and &lt; SKR = 90&deg;. If the length of the arc SR is four times that of arc PQ, find the length of the arc SR. [Take \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\)].</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Let &lt; POQ = \\(\\theta\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\implies\\) SR = \\(4\\theta\\).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(&lt; PSQ = \\frac{\\theta}{2} ; &lt; SPR = 2\\theta\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>In \\(\\Delta PSK\\),&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(2\\theta + \\frac{\\theta}{2} = 90&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{5\\theta}{2} = 90&deg; \\implies 5\\theta = 180&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = \\frac{180&deg;}{5} = 36&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore &lt; SOR = 4\\theta = 4 \\times 36&deg; = 144&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Length of arc = \\(\\frac{\\theta}{360&deg;} \\times 2\\pi r\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{144}{360} \\times 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(17.6 cm\\).</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
        "_page_idx": 3,
        "editor_images": [
            "/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan (2)(7).jpg"
        ]
    },
    "53270": {
        "order_id": 5,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "statistics",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>The table shows the number of suitcases possessed by a group of travellers.</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:50%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>No. of suitcases</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>5</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Travellers</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>9</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) Calculate the (i) median (ii) mean, correct to the nearest whole number.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Draw a bar chart to represent the information.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:50%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>x</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>5</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>9</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>fx</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>14</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>6</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>12</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>45</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(a)(i) Median = \\(\\frac{1}{2} (N + 1)\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{1}{2}(30 + 1) = 15.5\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 15th and 16th position</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{2 + 2}{2} = 2\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) Mean = \\(\\frac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(\\frac{84}{30}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(2.8 \\approxeq 3\\) (nearest whole no).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" /></p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 3,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 1,
