        "_page_idx": 2,
        "editor_images": null
    },
    "53305": {
        "order_id": 9,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "statistics",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>The marks obtained by 40 students in an examination are as follows :</p>\r\n\r\n<p>85 77 87 74 77 78 79 89 95 90 78 73 86 83 91 74 84 81 83 75 77 70 81 69 75 63 76 87 61 78 69 96 65 80 84 80 77 74 88 72.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) Copy and complete the table for the distribution using the above data.</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:60%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Class Boundaries</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Tally</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Frequency</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>59.5 - 64.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>64.5 - 69.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>69.5 - 74.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>74.5 - 79.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>79.5 - 84.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>84.5 - 89.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>89.5 - 94.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>94.5 - 99.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Draw a histogram to represent the distribution.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) Using your histogram, estimate the modal mark.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(d) If a student is chosen at random, find the probability that the student obtains a mark greater than 79.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:60%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Class Boundaries</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Tally</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>Frequency</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>59.5 - 64.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>||</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>64.5 - 69.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>|||</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>69.5 - 74.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td><s>||||</s>&nbsp;|</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>6</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>74.5 - 79.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td><s>||||</s>&nbsp;<s>||||</s>&nbsp;|</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>79.5 - 84.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td><s>||||</s>&nbsp;|||</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>8</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>84.5 - 89.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td><s>||||</s>&nbsp;||</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>89.5 - 94.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>||</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>94.5 - 99.5</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>|</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(b)&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (2).jpg\" style=\"height:371px; width:300px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>An histogram to represent the distribution of 40 students in an examination.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) Modal mark : \\(\\frac{74.5 + 79.5}{2} = \\frac{154}{2} = 77\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(d) Number of students who obtained marks greater than 79 : 8 + 7 + 2 + 1 = 18.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Total number of students = 40</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore\\) P(mark greater than 79) = \\(\\frac{18}{40} = \\frac{9}{20}\\)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 3,
        "editor_images": [
            "/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (2).jpg"
        ]
    },
    "53308": {
        "order_id": 10,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "triangles-and-polygons",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>In the diagram, PQT is a straight line and SQ // RT.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0253 (2).jpg\" style=\"height:129px; width:250px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) Join QR and show that : (i) &lt; RPS = &lt; QRT ; (ii) &lt; PRS = &lt; QTR.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) ABC is a triangle. The sides AB and AC are produced to D and E respectively such that &lt; DBC = 132&deg; and &lt; ECD = 96&deg;. Show that \\(\\Delta\\) ABC is isosceles.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a) &lt; QRT = &lt; RQS (alternate angles)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&lt; RPS = &lt; RQS (angles in the same segment)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore\\) &lt; RPS = &lt; QRT</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) &lt; QRT = &lt; PQS (corresponding angles)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&lt; PQS = &lt; PRS (angles in the same segment)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore\\) &lt; QTR = &lt; PRS.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) \\(&lt; ABC = \\hat{B} = 180&deg; - 132&deg; = 48&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(&lt; ACB = \\hat{C} = 180&deg; - 96&deg; = 84&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(&lt; BAC = \\hat{A} = 180&deg; - (48&deg; + 84&deg;) = 48&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(&lt; BAC = &lt; ABC = 48&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore \\Delta ABC = isosceles\\).</p>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (3)_LI.jpg\" style=\"height:288px; width:300px\" /></p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 2,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 2,
        "_page_idx": 4,
        "editor_images": [
            "/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0253 (2).jpg",
            "/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (3)_LI.jpg"
        ]
    },
    "53311": {
        "order_id": 11,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "geometry-and-trigonometry",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>An aeroplane flies due west for 3 hours from P (lat. 50&deg;N, long. 60&deg;W) to a point Q at an average speed of 600km/h. The aeroplane then flies due south from Q to a point Y 500km away. Calculate, correct to 3 significant figures,&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) the longitude of Q ;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) the latitude of Y . [Take the radius of the earth = 6400km and \\(\\pi = \\frac{22}{7}\\)].</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a)&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (4).jpg\" style=\"height:165px; width:250px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{r}{R} = \\cos 50\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(r = 6400 \\cos 50 = 4,113.84 km\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\approxeq 4,114km\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The distance PQ along the parallel of latitude = speed (km/h) \\(\\times\\) time (h)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 600km/h x 3h</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= 1800km</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\theta}{360} \\times 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r = 1800\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = \\frac{1800 \\times 7 \\times 360}{44 \\times 4113.84}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = 25.059&deg; \\approxeq 25.1&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore\\) The longitude of Q = \\(60 + \\theta\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>= \\(60 + 25.1 = 85.1&deg;W\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) The distance (Q) along the meridian</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\theta}{360} \\times 2\\pi R\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(500 = \\frac{\\theta}{360} \\times 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 6400\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = \\frac{500 \\times 360 \\times 7}{44 \\times 6400}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\theta = 4.47&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore \\text{The latitude of Y} = 50&deg; - 4.47&deg; = 45.53&deg;\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\approxeq 45.5&deg;N\\)</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [],
        "_page_num": 3,
        "_page_idx": 0,
        "editor_images": [
            "/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0255 (4).jpg"
        ]
    },
    "53312": {
