    "53313": {
        "order_id": 13,
        "exam_type": "WAEC",
        "subject": "Mathematics",
        "topic": "graph-of-linear-and-quadratic-functions",
        "question_type": "Theory",
        "exam_year": "2003",
        "question_text": "<p>The table below shows the values of the relation \\(y = 11 - 2x - 2x^{2}\\) for \\(-4 \\leq x \\leq 3\\).</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:50%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>x</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>y</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-13</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(a) Copy and complete the table.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(b) Using a scale of 2 cm to 1 unit on the x- axis and 2 cm to 5 units on the y- axis, draw the graph of \\(y = 11 - 2x - 2x^{2}\\).</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c) Use your graph to find : (i) the roots of the equation \\(11 - 2x - 2x^{2} = 0\\) ; (ii) the values of x for which \\(3 - 2x - 2x^{2} = 0\\) ; (iii) the gradient of the curve at x = 1.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>(a)&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:50%\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>x</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-3</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>3</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\\(x^{2}\\)</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>16</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>9</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>9</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\\(11\\)</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\\(-2x\\)</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>8</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>6</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-4</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-6</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>\\(-2x^{2}\\)</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-32</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-18</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-8</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>0</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-2</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-8</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-18</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td>y</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-13</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>11</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>7</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-1</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>-13</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>(b)&nbsp;<img alt=\"\" src=\"/db/nigeria/exam_image/editor_images/WAEC/Mathematics/2003/scan0257 (2).jpg\" style=\"height:389px; width:300px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(c)(i) x = -2.9 or 1.9</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) \\(y + (3 - 2x - 2x^{2}) = 11 - 2x - 2x^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(y = 11 - 2x - 2x^{2} - 3 + 2x + 2x^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(y = 8\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\therefore x = \\text{-1.8 or 0.8}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(iii) \\(y = 11 - 2x - 2x^{2}\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\\(\\frac{\\mathrm d y}{\\mathrm d x} = -2 - 4x\\)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Gradient at x = 1 : \\(-2 - 4(1) = -2 - 4 = -6\\)</p>",
